  <title id="bdlsamplerpaths-title">Random-walk Metropolis and Hamiltonian Monte Carlo on a correlated two-dimensional Gaussian</title>
  <desc id="bdlsamplerpaths-desc">Both samplers start at the same point in the lower left of a narrow Gaussian whose ellipses lie along the diagonal. With 120 proposals, random-walk Metropolis moves in short steps and covers only a small part of the long axis. With the same number of gradient evaluations, Hamiltonian Monte Carlo makes 8 transitions whose leapfrog trajectories, drawn dashed, sweep along the ellipse, so its 8 states spread along most of the long axis, while the random walk stays in the lower half.</desc>
